{"path":"memory/polymorphic_allocator/operator_eq","title":"std::pmr::operator==, std::pmr::operator!=","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::pmr::</span>operator==, <span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::pmr::</span>operator!=","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/polymorphic_allocator/operator_eq","section":"memory","kind":"page","summary":"Compares two polymorphic allocators. Two polymorphic allocators compare equal if their underlying memory resource compares equal.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/memory_resource\">&lt;memory_resource&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx17\" id=\"Version_1\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> T1, <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> T2 <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br><span class=\"kw4\">bool</span> operator<span class=\"sy1\">==</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/polymorphic_allocator\"><span class=\"kw711\">std::<span class=\"me2\">pmr</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">polymorphic_allocator</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T1<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> lhs,<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/polymorphic_allocator\"><span class=\"kw711\">std::<span class=\"me2\">pmr</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">polymorphic_allocator</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T2<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> rhs <span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (1) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx17\">(since C++17)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx17\" id=\"Version_2\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">friend</span> <span class=\"kw4\">bool</span> operator<span class=\"sy1\">==</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> polymorphic_allocator<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> lhs,<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> polymorphic_allocator<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> rhs <span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (2) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx17\">(since C++17)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx17 t-until-cxx20\" id=\"Version_3\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> T1, <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> T2 <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br><span class=\"kw4\">bool</span> operator<span class=\"sy3\">!</span><span class=\"sy1\">=</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/polymorphic_allocator\"><span class=\"kw711\">std::<span class=\"me2\">pmr</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">polymorphic_allocator</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T1<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> lhs,<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/polymorphic_allocator\"><span class=\"kw711\">std::<span class=\"me2\">pmr</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">polymorphic_allocator</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T2<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> rhs <span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (3) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx17\">(since C++17)</span> <br><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-until-cxx20\">(until C++20)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx17 t-until-cxx20\" id=\"Version_4\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">friend</span> <span class=\"kw4\">bool</span> operator<span class=\"sy3\">!</span><span class=\"sy1\">=</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> polymorphic_allocator<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> lhs,<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> polymorphic_allocator<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> rhs <span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (4) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx17\">(since C++17)</span> <br><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-until-cxx20\">(until C++20)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Compares two polymorphic allocators. Two polymorphic allocators compare equal if their underlying memory resource compares equal.\n</p>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1)</span> Returns <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>lhs.<span class=\"me1\">resource</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <span class=\"sy2\">*</span>rhs.<span class=\"me1\">resource</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">2)</span> Same as <span class=\"t-v\">(1)</span>, allowing conversion to <code>polymorphic_allocator</code>.<br>This function  is not visible to ordinary <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/unqualified_lookup\">unqualified</a> or <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/qualified_lookup\">qualified lookup</a>, and can only be found by <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/adl\">argument-dependent lookup</a> when std::pmr::polymorphic_allocator is an associated class of the arguments.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">3)</span> Returns <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy3\">!</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>lhs <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> rhs<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">4)</span> Same as <span class=\"t-v\">(3)</span>, allowing conversion to <code>polymorphic_allocator</code>.<br>This function  is not visible to ordinary <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/unqualified_lookup\">unqualified</a> or <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/qualified_lookup\">qualified lookup</a>, and can only be found by <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/adl\">argument-dependent lookup</a> when std::pmr::polymorphic_allocator is an associated class of the arguments.</div>\n<table class=\"t-rev-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-rev t-since-cxx20\"><td>\n<p>The <code>!=</code> operator is <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/default_comparisons#Other_defaulted_comparison_operators\">synthesized</a> from <code>operator==</code>.\n</p>\n</td>\n<td><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(since C++20)</span></td></tr>\n</table>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> lhs, rhs\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> polymorphic allocators to compare\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1,2)</span> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>lhs.<span class=\"me1\">resource</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <span class=\"sy2\">*</span>rhs.<span class=\"me1\">resource</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code></div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">3,4)</span> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy3\">!</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>lhs <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> rhs<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code></div>\n<h3 id=\"Defect_reports\">Defect reports</h3>\n<p>The following behavior-changing defect reports were applied retroactively to previously published C++ standards.\n</p>\n<table class=\"dsctable\">\n<tr>\n<th>DR\n</th>\n<th>Applied to\n</th>\n<th>Behavior as published\n</th>\n<th>Correct behavior\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cplusplus.github.io/LWG/issue3683\" data-external=\"1\">LWG 3683</a>\n</td>\n<td>C++17\n</td>\n<td><code>polymorphic_allocator</code> could not be compared with types convertible to it\n</td>\n<td>overload added\n</td></tr></table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Defect reports","id":"Defect_reports"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"memory","title":"Memory management library"},{"path":"memory/polymorphic_allocator","title":"std::pmr::polymorphic_allocator"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::pmr::operator==, std::pmr::operator!=","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"4 declarations; revisions: since C++17, until C++20. Compares two polymorphic allocators."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"lhs, rhs"},{"label":"Return value","note":"*lhs.resource() == *rhs.resource()"},{"label":"Defect reports","note":"The following behavior-changing defect reports were applied retroactively to previously published C++ standards."}]},"standards":["C++17","C++20"],"wordCount":233,"codeBlockCount":0}
